  <subsection xml:id="subsec-sec-a-6-practice-problems-factoring-and-completing-the-square">
    <title>Factoring and completing the square</title>

    <ol>
      <li>
        <p>Factor <m>x^2+7x+12</m>.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>Factor <m>2x^2-5x-3</m>.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>Factor <m>x^3-8</m>.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>Complete the square:</p>
          <md>x^2+10x+13.</md>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>Complete the square:</p>
          <md>3x^2-12x+7.</md>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>Solve:</p>
          <md>x^2-4x-5=0.</md>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </subsection>

  <subsection xml:id="subsec-sec-a-6-practice-problems-rational-expressions">
    <title>Rational expressions</title>

    <ol>
      <li>
        <p>Simplify:</p>
          <md>\frac{x^2-4}{x-2}.</md>
        <p>State the restriction.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>Simplify:</p>
          <md>\frac{x^2+3x+2}{x^2-1}.</md>
        <p>State the restrictions.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>Simplify:</p>
          <md>\frac{1}{x}+\frac{1}{x+2}.</md>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>Simplify:</p>
          <md>\frac{\frac1{x+h}-\frac1x}{h},
\qquad h\neq0.</md>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>Rationalize:</p>
          <md>\frac{\sqrt{x+9}-3}{x}.</md>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </subsection>

  <subsection xml:id="subsec-sec-a-6-practice-problems-exponents-and-radicals">
    <title>Exponents and radicals</title>

    <ol>
      <li>
        <p>Rewrite as a power of <m>x</m>:</p>
          <md>\frac{1}{x^3\sqrt{x}}.</md>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>Simplify:</p>
          <md>x^{2/3}x^{5/3}.</md>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>Rewrite using radicals:</p>
          <md>x^{3/2}.</md>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>Simplify:</p>
          <md>\left(x^{-2}\right)^3.</md>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>State the real domain of</p>
          <md>\frac{1}{\sqrt{x-4}}.</md>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </subsection>

  <subsection xml:id="subsec-sec-a-6-practice-problems-inequalities-and-absolute-values">
    <title>Inequalities and absolute values</title>

    <ol>
      <li>
        <p>Solve:</p>
          <md>5-2x\le 11.</md>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>Solve:</p>
          <md>x^2+x-6&lt;0.</md>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>Solve:</p>
          <md>\frac{x-4}{x+1}&gt;0.</md>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>Solve:</p>
          <md>|x-3|&lt;0.5.</md>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>Solve:</p>
          <md>|4x-1|\ge 7.</md>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </subsection>

  <subsection xml:id="subsec-sec-a-6-practice-problems-sigma-notation">
    <title>Sigma notation</title>

    <ol>
      <li>
        <p>Expand:</p>
          <md>\sum_{k=1}^{5}(k^2+1).</md>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>Compute:</p>
          <md>\sum_{k=1}^{20} k.</md>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>Compute:</p>
          <md>\sum_{k=1}^{6} k^2.</md>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>Compute:</p>
          <md>\sum_{k=0}^{5} 2^k.</md>
      </li>
      <li>
